      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hamorton's 1830s layout survives today, with narrow Ash and Pine alleys flanking the original Baltimore Pike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.livingplaces.com/PA/Chester_County/Kennett_Township/Hamorton_Historic_District.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 1920s duPont widened Baltimore Pike, sacrificing Abraham Hamor’s 1830s store to create the road’s modern width.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.livingplaces.com/PA/Chester_County/Kennett_Township/Hamorton_Historic_District.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Route 1 and Route 52 cross in Hamorton, placing the town just three miles east of Chadds Ford and ten miles southeast of Wilmington.",
